From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 07:00:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ofono: bring the interface of an active context up

Restarting connmand while oFono kept a data context up left the phone
without mobile data: the cellular service showed "ready", then failed
its online check with "could not resolve", and there were no routes at
all. The context's interface (ccmni0 on a MediaTek modem) was down.

connmand takes every running interface down when it starts, in
cleanup_devices(), on the understanding that it brings them up again
itself. For cellular it never does: the modem's driver brings the
interface up when it sets up a data call, and the oFono device has no
interface of its own. A context that is already active when connmand
starts is adopted by set_connected(), which applied the address,
routes and nameservers to a link that stayed down.

Bring the interface up in set_connected(), as the dundee plugin does
for its own. An interface the modem already brought up is left as it
is.

unit/test-ofono compiles plugins/ofono.c with the core stubbed and
checks that set_connected() brings the interface up before it connects
the network, also when the interface is already up, and does neither
without an interface.

Seen on a Q25 when connmand was restarted with Vodafone NL data up.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 Makefile.am       |  11 ++
 plugins/ofono.c   |  11 ++
 unit/test-ofono.c | 287 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 309 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 unit/test-ofono.c

diff --git a/Makefile.am b/Makefile.am
index db66854..5b96ed0 100644
--- a/Makefile.am
+++ b/Makefile.am
@@ -618,3 +618,14 @@ maintainer-clean-local:
 
 clean-local:
 	@$(RM) -rf include/connman $(MANUAL_PAGES)
+
+# The oFono plugin compiled into its test, with the core stubbed there.
+# At the end of the file so that it stays clear of the other unit tests.
+noinst_PROGRAMS += unit/test-ofono
+
+unit_test_ofono_SOURCES = $(backtrace_sources) src/log.c \
+				plugins/mcc.h unit/test-ofono.c
+unit_test_ofono_LDADD = gdbus/libgdbus-internal.la \
+				@GLIB_LIBS@ @DBUS_LIBS@ -ldl
+
+TESTS += unit/test-ofono
diff --git a/plugins/ofono.c b/plugins/ofono.c
index 567c0d3..7320241 100644
--- a/plugins/ofono.c
+++ b/plugins/ofono.c
@@ -309,6 +309,17 @@ static void set_connected(struct modem_data *modem,
 
 	DBG("context->network %p", context->network);
 
+	/*
+	 * The modem's driver normally brings the interface up when the
+	 * data call is set up, but connmand takes every running interface
+	 * down when it starts (cleanup_devices() in src/device.c). A
+	 * context that oFono still reports active from before a restart
+	 * would then get its address on a link that stays down, with no
+	 * routes and no traffic. An active context needs its interface up,
+	 * as dundee does for its own.
+	 */
+	connman_inet_ifup(index);
+
 	service = connman_service_lookup_from_network(context->network);
 	if (!service)
 		return;
diff --git a/unit/test-ofono.c b/unit/test-ofono.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f2ea163
--- /dev/null
+++ b/unit/test-ofono.c
@@ -0,0 +1,287 @@
